B.S7=new A.fL("Julius Caesar","100\u201344 BC",'Ancient historians including Suetonius and Plutarch describe episodes of "falling sickness." Modern historians and physicians continue to debate whether this reflected epilepsy, another medical condition, or was partly political characterization \u2014 an unresolved retrospective question, not a confirmed diagnosis.',B.fg)
B.Sc=new A.fL("Vincent van Gogh","1853\u20131890","Van Gogh's physicians and later scholars have proposed numerous, competing explanations for his psychiatric and physical crises, including temporal lobe epilepsy, bipolar disorder and other conditions. No single diagnosis is settled, and epilepsy remains one hypothesis among several.",B.fg)
B.S8=new A.fL("Joan of Arc","c. 1412\u20131431","Some historians and neurologists have speculated that Joan of Arc's visions could be consistent with a temporal lobe epilepsy aura. This is a retrospective hypothesis debated among historians, not a confirmed diagnosis by any contemporary or modern clinical standard.",B.fg)
B.Sb=new A.fL("Alexander the Great","356\u2013323 BC","Ancient sources describe convulsive collapses attributed to Alexander. As with other ancient figures, this is debated by historians and cannot be confirmed as epilepsy by modern criteria.",B.fg)
