B.Fh=new A.ch("Epilepsy vs PNES","Lateral tongue bite","Strongly favors a generalized tonic-clonic epileptic seizure over PNES.",B.cz)
B.F0=new A.ch("Epilepsy vs PNES","Forced eye closure","Forced or resisted eye closure during the event favors PNES \u2014 eyes are open in most epileptic seizures.",B.cz)
B.Fo=new A.ch("Epilepsy vs PNES","Todd's paralysis","Strongly supports a focal epileptic seizure and is rarely, if ever, seen in PNES.",B.cz)
B.bX=new A.yw(1,"supportive")
B.F1=new A.ch("Epilepsy vs PNES","Asynchronous limb movements","Out-of-phase limb thrashing favors PNES; epileptic clonic activity is typically synchronous and rhythmic.",B.bX)
B.F2=new A.ch("Epilepsy vs PNES","Immediate full recovery","Recovery without postictal confusion argues against a generalized epileptic seizure.",B.bX)
B.Fa=new A.ch("Epilepsy vs PNES","Post-ictal prolactin","A normal level after a witnessed convulsive event favors PNES; a rise at 10-20 minutes favors epilepsy.",B.bX)
B.e2=new A.yw(2,"expert")
B.Fi=new A.ch("Epilepsy vs PNES","Dual diagnosis is common","PNES and epilepsy frequently coexist in the same patient \u2014 diagnosing one does not exclude the other.",B.e2)
B.F5=new A.ch("Epilepsy vs PNES","Prolonged event duration","Events lasting many minutes with preserved oxygenation are more typical of PNES; most epileptic seizures self-terminate within 1-2 minutes.",B.bX)
B.Fn=new A.ch("Localization","D\xe9j\xe0 vu & epigastric aura","D\xe9j\xe0 vu, epigastric rising, and oroalimentary automatisms usually suggest temporal lobe onset.",B.cz)
B.Fm=new A.ch("Localization","Figure-of-4 & fencing posture","Both lateralize to a supplementary motor area (frontal) seizure, contralateral to the extended arm.",B.cz)
B.Ff=new A.ch("Localization","Clustered nocturnal seizures","Brief, frequent, clustered nocturnal seizures with rapid recovery point toward a frontal lobe origin.",B.bX)
B.Fd=new A.ch("Localization","Elementary visual hallucinations","Flashing lights suggest occipital onset; slower, spreading, colored scintillations suggest migraine instead.",B.bX)
B.Fp=new A.ch("Localization","Choking sensation & dysautonomia","Painful unilateral paresthesia with dysautonomia and a choking sensation should raise suspicion for insular onset.",B.bX)
B.Fg=new A.ch("Localization","MRI-negative frontal epilepsy","Frontal lobe seizures are frequently MRI-negative even when focal cortical dysplasia is the underlying cause.",B.e2)
B.Fk=new A.ch("Syndromes","Gelastic seizures","Suggest a hypothalamic hamartoma, especially with precocious puberty in a child.",B.cz)
B.F7=new A.ch("Syndromes","Early-morning myoclonus","Ask every adolescent with early-morning myoclonic jerks about juvenile myoclonic epilepsy before labeling episodes as clumsiness.",B.cz)
B.F4=new A.ch("Syndromes","Infantile spasms","With developmental regression, a pediatric neurologic emergency requiring urgent EEG (hypsarrhythmia) and treatment.",B.cz)
B.F8=new A.ch("Syndromes","Catamenial pattern","Best confirmed with a seizure diary correlated against a menstrual calendar, not by history alone.",B.e2)
B.Fb=new A.ch("Syndromes","Reflex epilepsy triggers","Photosensitive, reading, musicogenic, hot water and startle epilepsies share a stereotyped trigger-to-seizure relationship \u2014 ask specifically.",B.bX)
B.Fj=new A.ch("Mimics","Convulsive syncope","The single most commonly misdiagnosed seizure mimic in adults \u2014 look for a presyncopal prodrome and rapid full recovery.",B.cz)
B.F6=new A.ch("Mimics","Anoxic myoclonus","Brief myoclonic jerks during a faint do not make an event epileptic.",B.bX)
B.F9=new A.ch("Mimics","Bedside glucose","Always check during the acute evaluation of any transient event \u2014 hypoglycemia is a readily reversible mimic.",B.e2)
B.Fe=new A.ch("Mimics","Migraine aura tempo","Migraine with aura evolves more slowly (minutes) than an epileptic aura (seconds) and is usually followed by headache.",B.bX)
B.Fl=new A.ch("Investigations","Normal EEG \u2260 no epilepsy","A single normal interictal EEG does not exclude epilepsy \u2014 sensitivity rises with sleep-deprived and repeated recordings.",B.e2)
B.Fc=new A.ch("Investigations","Video-EEG monitoring","Capturing a typical habitual event remains the diagnostic gold standard when the differential is unclear.",B.e2)
B.F3=new A.ch("Investigations","CK & lactate rise","Elevated CK and a transient venous lactate rise support a recent convulsive epileptic seizure.",B.bX)
